{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.13", "U6.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The SKW92A module pins 13 and 14 are tied directly to the GND net. In the library part, those pins are named LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- and are bidirectional Ethernet differential signals, not ground pins.",
      "expected": "Ethernet PHY differential signal pins should not be shorted directly to ground unless the datasheet or intended design explicitly specifies that connection. The specification notes that the RJ45 jack is unconnected, but it does not state that the module's LAN3 transmit pair is grounded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart (lib \"SKW92A\") (part \"SKW92A\") ... (pin (num \"13\") (name \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (type \"bidirectional\")) (pin (num \"14\") (name \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (type \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "In this netlist export, the Ethernet jack is not wired to the SKW92A's Ethernet PHY nets."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the Ethernet PHY is enabled, the LAN3 transmit differential pair is shorted to ground, which can cause excessive current, possible damage, or incorrect Ethernet behavior. Even if the port is unused, this is an undocumented direct tie of bidirectional signal pins to ground.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C5"],
      "pins": ["C5.1", "C5.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C5-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C5 is declared as a 0.1 uF capacitor, but its footprint is an inductor footprint, and pin 1 is on a one-pin unconnected net while pin 2 is connected to GND.",
      "expected": "A decoupling or bypass capacitor in the power section should be connected across a supply rail and ground and should use a capacitor footprint. A floating capacitor pin indicates a missing connection or a copy/footprint error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C5\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C5-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"C5\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C5\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended high-frequency decoupling is not present because one terminal is floating. The mismatched inductor footprint also suggests a possible sourcing or assembly error.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most spec-critical connectivity matches, but the netlist shows two deviations: the SKW92A LAN3 transmit differential pair is tied directly to ground, and a 0.1 uF capacitor in the power section is left floating with an inductor footprint."
}

